# RouteComposer

Single A → B walkable pathfinder used by **every** route in the engine — `player`, `default`, `seat_nav`, `find_my_seat`, `find_toilets`, `quiet_zone_nav`, `poi_nav` (bird-eye). Given two world positions, produces one `ComposedRoute` covering any combination of NavMesh "islands" and the OSM city graph: same-island NavMesh, NavMesh → OSM, OSM → NavMesh, OSM → OSM, or cross-island NavMesh → OSM → NavMesh.

The route engine no longer has separate "raw NavMesh", "multi-segment via-points", or "measure breakdown" branches — those behaviours are now selected by passing the right keyword arguments to `compose()`:

| Behaviour | How |
|---|---|
| Crowd / quiet-zone cost-aware NavMesh leg | `camera_area_costs={...}`, `sound_area_costs={...}` |
| Multi-segment via-point legs (POI, search) | `via_points=[(x,y,z), …]` |
| Auto corridor routing for intra-island routes | `enable_corridor_routing=True` (bird-eye opt-in) |
| Cancel mid-compose (point-and-click thread) | `is_stale=lambda: my_gen != self._gen` |
| Base / actual / crowd-delta / sound-delta UI | `compose_with_measure(...)` wrapper in `measure.py` |

There is no `_compute_via_composer` / `_compute_multi_segment` / `compute_route_measure` engine branch. One pathfinder, one configurable surface.

**Home**: `kit-app-template-main/source/extensions/younite.navmesh_route_extension/younite/navmesh_route_extension/services/kit_services/route_composer/`

| Submodule | Role |
|---|---|
| `composer.py` | `RouteComposer` class + private case handlers (`_same_navmesh`, `_navmesh_to_osm`, `_osm_to_navmesh`, `_osm_to_osm`, `_cross_navmesh`, `_finalize`) and the per-call `_ComposeContext` options bundle |
| `osm.py` | `OsmLegPlanner` — `OsmGraphService` wrapper + cached `/World/OSM_Roads` offset + Dijkstra leg + forward-bias probe |
| `measure.py` | `compose_with_measure()` — runs `compose()` 1-3 times to build the base / actual / crowd-delta / sound-delta breakdown the seat / find-toilets / quiet-zone UI consumes |
| `types.py` | `ComposedLeg` / `ComposedRoute` dataclasses + tunable constants |
| `geometry.py` | Shared math helpers (`xz_dist2`, `is_segment_on_navmesh`, `dedupe_close`, `trim_leading_backtrack`, `trim_trailing_backtrack`) |
| `registry.py` | Process-wide singleton: `get_route_composer()` / `set_route_composer()` / `set_route_service()` |
| `__init__.py` | Re-exports the public API |

---

## Why a single pathfinder

Earlier the route engine had four parallel branches doing roughly the same job (raw `calculate_path_points`, multi-segment via-points, `compute_route_measure`, and the composer fast-path) — every bird-eye bug had to be re-fixed in the "normal" code paths and vice versa. The user explicitly called this out: "we are STILL using separate solutions and building duplicate code." The unification collapses those four into one entry point so a fix in `RouteComposer` benefits every route type.

Behavioural mapping after the unification:

| Route id | `via_points` | `enable_corridor_routing` | `is_stale` | Costs | Measure |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `player` (point-click) | None | False | yes (worker thread) | merged | None |
| `default` | None | False | None | merged | base/actual |
| `seat_nav` / `find_my_seat` | corridor pts (extension.py) | False | None | merged | base/actual/delta |
| `find_toilets` / `quiet_zone_nav` | corridor pts | False | None | merged | base/actual/delta |
| `poi_nav` (bird-eye) | None (composer auto-corridor) | True | None | merged | base/actual/delta |

The composer doesn't know about route ids — only about the options dict. The route engine maps each route to the right combination.

