## Data types

```python
@dataclass
class ComposedLeg:
    kind: str               # "navmesh" or "osm"
    island: Optional[str]   # e.g. "scandinavium"; None for OSM legs
    points: List[Vec3]      # >= 2 world-space points
    edge_classes: List[str] # len == len(points) - 1; "navmesh"/"bridge" for NavMesh legs, OSM class strings for OSM legs

@dataclass
class ComposedRoute:
    legs: List[ComposedLeg]
    polyline: List[Vec3]          # flat stitched polyline (shared boundaries deduped)
    segment_speeds: List[float]   # per-segment speed multiplier; len == len(polyline) - 1
    segment_classes: List[str]    # per-segment path class parallel to segment_speeds
    start_island: Optional[str]
    end_island: Optional[str]
```

**Convenience properties** (computed on read):

| Property | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `has_navmesh` / `has_osm` | Predicates for quick branching |
| `navmesh_points` / `osm_points` | All NavMesh / OSM points concatenated — feeds the two `BirdEyeRouteProjector` channels |
| `distance_cm` / `distance_meters` | Sum of XZ segment lengths — used for `navmeshRouteMeasure` |
| `estimated_time_seconds` | Honours `segment_speeds` and `DEFAULT_WALK_SPEED_M_PER_S` |

### `segment_classes`

Parallel to `segment_speeds`, one class string per segment. Possible values:

| Class | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `navmesh` | NavMesh leg segment |
| `bridge` | Synthetic segment connecting a NavMesh leg to an adjacent OSM leg (the entrance → first-OSM-node handover) |
| `pedestrian` / `steps` / `residential` / `arterial` / `highway` | OSM edge class — matches `OsmGraphService.path_to_edge_classes()` |

`PointClickAutoMover` consumes this channel to detect path-class transitions at runtime (e.g. `navmesh → bridge → pedestrian → residential`) and dispatches `playerPathClassChange { prev, next, segIdx, routeId }`. See `osm-navigation.mdc` for the event contract.

