## Failure modes

All return `None` from `compose()` (or `(None, None)` from `compose_with_measure()`):

| Failure | Cause |
|---|---|
| NavMesh leg failed | `calculate_path_points` returned `success=False` (endpoint off-mesh, query disconnected) |
| OSM graph unavailable | `OsmGraphService.load()` failed or the graph is not yet loaded |
| No OSM path | `shortest_path()` returned empty / zero-distance (endpoints disconnected in the graph) |
| No entrance in scope | `_scan_entrances()` returned empty for the required island |
| Stale | `is_stale()` callback returned True before the next leg started |

Callers either dispatch a visible error (`navmeshRouteError`, `birdEyePinError`) or just lift the view-transition overlay and let the user try again.

