## Adding a new A → B navigation feature

The composer is the only pathfinder. Pattern for any future "walk from A to B" flow:

```python
composer = get_route_composer()
composed = composer.compose(
    start_world, end_world,
    camera_area_costs=cam, sound_area_costs=snd,  # optional cost overrides
    via_points=via,                               # optional corridor pts
    enable_corridor_routing=True,                 # optional auto-corridor
)
if composed is None:
    return  # handle failure

# Auto-mover dispatch — works for any route shape, no branching needed.
dispatch_to_events2("navmeshRouteWaypoints", {
    "routeId": my_route_id,
    "success": True,
    "points": [list(p) for p in composed.polyline],
    "segmentSpeeds": composed.segment_speeds,
    "segmentClasses": composed.segment_classes,  # opt-in; enables playerPathClassChange
})
```

If the feature wires into the route engine via `set_route_for_id`, just pass the right options and `_compute_path` will use them.

